        <figcaption><b>The commit is the trigger, and the checkpoint is a sibling of your branch, not part of it.</b> Each checkpoint is an independent ref — sharded by the last two characters of its ULID — so concurrent agent sessions write, push and fetch without contending over a shared branch, and your branch history stays clean. The <code>Entire-Checkpoint:</code> trailer is the only trace in the commit itself, which is also the link you hand a judge.</figcaption>
